A||||29||Robert||The most significant cars you have owned and why?||||5||
Z||000000||Robert||07-29-2001||11:33 PM||||I was just thinking back to all the cars I’ve owned in my life, and what made them that way.  I’m sure most of us (sorry to all the youngsters in the group) have owned many cars in our lives, but we didn’t know which one’s would be the significant ones when we bought them. <BR>Here is a list of my significant cars and what made them that way.<P>How about you?<P>1954 Chevrolet station wagon -<BR>	This was my first car.  Bought it at age 16 in 1964 for $50.00 (piece of junk, broke a pushrod every few days).  Didn’t tell my mother (single mom) and when she did find out she made me sell it quick.<P>1961? Rambler American –<BR>	Bought it in 1967.  First car I ever “made whoopee” in.   Gotta love those tilt down seats at the drive-in.<P>1977? Plymouth minivan -<BR>	My first brand new car; had a family now and needed room.<P>1988 Pontiac Trans Am GTA T-Tops -<BR>	Bought it in 1990.  Turned 40, just got divorced, needed a something to boost my self-image.<P>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT -<BR>	Bought it in 1999, been remarried for 5 years now, life is good, could care less about my image, through this car have made many new friends.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">   <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."||||reg||5
Z||000001||HummelHund||07-30-2001||12:30 AM||||Ok here goes, all my cars and their respective significances. Keep in mind I'm only 17, yet I've owned 5 cars. And before any of you adult type people say anything, none have been wrecked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>1. 1979 MGB : My kind and caring father bought this car for me when I was about 14, we were to restore it. Words of wisdom- never buy a car that's been "partially disassembled" or "ran when parked". The car never ran when I had it. Significance- I learned the many quirks of British wiring. Sold.<P>2. 1987 Merkur XR4Ti: Yet another parental gift, a beauty of a car, all black with that cool biplane spoiler. We thought all that was wrong was an ignition module. Turned out to be a broken crankshaft. Ah well. Significance- Taught me never to buy a car that you can't hear at least attempt to run. Sold, but we still have an 89' XR, they're great cars, almost as weird as Fieros.<P>3. 1986 Audi Coupe GT: Free hand me down from my brother. Needed lots of stuff, mostly due to his incompetent driving. Great car, but I was destined for greater things. Significance- Never let your brother drive your future car. Disconnect something so it doesn't run. Sold.<P>4. 1991 Mercury Capri Convertible: Great fun driving with the top down. But the windows didn't work. Trim pieces fell off at random, as if abandoning ship. The worst built car I have ever driven. Still, it was fun until that cold night when the top wouldn't go up, and I ripped a huge hole in it. It was slower than an Iron Duke Fiero. 'Nuff said. Significance: Don't buy anything built by 3 companies in 3 countries. Sold to buy...<P>5. 1984 Pontiac Fiero SE: The greatest car ever. I rescued it for $400 out of some weeds in a man's backyard. So it's been in a period of rehabilitation since I bought it, it's coming along nicely. I've poured $1100 in parts into this car, along with about 3 pints of blood during the throttle cable installation. Should be on the road soon. It runs and shifts now, only a few minor pieces and I can impress my friends at school by yelling "Oh my Lord, someone's stolen my engine!!!" while pointing to the front trunk. Significance- Working on the Fiero has taught me a great deal about working on cars, and it's fun!<P>Hopefully someday I'll be able to add a fastback GT to that list, but for now I'm content with my little "buzz bomb". <P><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe, The "Black Wedge of Death" ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||07-30-2001||12:58 AM||||My significant cars... hmmmm... well, all of them in some way probably. I've had hundreds but what comes to mind right off...<P>76 Plymouth Roadrunner - first car<BR>84 Porsche 911 - dream car<BR>69 Ram Air IV Judge - muscle car!!!<BR>80 Fiat X1/9 - first convertible and it hooked me<BR>V12 Jaguar XJS-HE - Class and a V12!<P>So many others could be here, but I've listed some of them before so won't bore you again...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||07-30-2001||01:05 AM||||Not counting my current 84se...<P>1985 Camaro Z28 -<BR>Personally installed Edlbrock cam, lfters, intake manifold, carb, heads, roller rockers, firebal pushrods, double roller timing chain, changed the distributor back from computer controlled to vaccum advance, braided line hoses, trans shift kit, and then some. Lost when a Suburban rear ended me.<P>1987 Fiero Coupe - My first real Fiero experience. Ended when I decided to help jack up a Subaru impressa sedan... With my front end.<P>1990 Eclipse GS - Did some custom work to this, and was my first import experience.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||07-30-2001||02:13 AM||||My cars.<P>1984 Fiero - First car was fun and scary to drie at the same time. It had lots of problems but none of them kept it from being driven daily. Though some of them should have.<P>1979 Chevy Sport van - a big change from a Fiero. The car that I've owned the longest. Mostly becase it's rotting in my driveway after I severely overheated it during a huge snowstorm. I wasn't about to get out and walk. Drove it home on 5 cylinders the next day too.<P>1987 Mazda GLC 4 door. Got it for free becase the lady who owned it wanted it out of her yard and I figured I could make a few bucks. Even though she said that it needed a new alternator and water pump, they were both fine. I sold it to the lady's daughter a month later for $300 and all i did was bleed the brakes. From then on, I don't believe anyone who says that Japaneese cars are made better. There was nothing about that car that said quality.<P>1987 Pontiac Trans Am - First relatively fast car. Because of it, I will NEVER buy another car with t-tops again. While the body and most of the driveline were in great shape, the rest of the car was falling apart, mostly because of the t-tops leaking and humidifying the interior. The car was heavily abused before I bought it. Though it had low miles because someone glued the numbers on the odometer together. It was a bad buy for the $1600 i paid for it, but a great deal for the kid who i sold it to at a $1000 loss   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>1986 Fiero GT - Finally got me a GT. I drove it 120 miles with bald rear tires, and no plates or insurance to get it home. Somehow I'm not in jail right now. I put about $3000 into it and you can't tell from looking at it. It's faster than my 84, but somehow, not as fun. I might find me a cheap coupe and throw the upgrades that I can take off of my GT on to it.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jaygee79||07-30-2001||09:27 AM||||Well, the only car I've ever owned is my Fiero, so I guess that would be it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooh14.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||07-30-2001||09:31 AM||||Fiat X1/9 - it's the reason I own a Fiero now.||||reg||14
Z||000007||Raydar||07-30-2001||09:53 AM||||68 Ford Fairlane 500. My "first" car that wasn't a hand-me-down. Got it at age 16 in '73. Broke 2 or 3 transmissions, the rear end, and the frame. Long story.<P>71 Barracuda. First stick-shift car. Learned to drive a stick shift on the way home.<P>76 Chevy Monza. 350 4-speed. Installed the 350/300 HP from a 70 Impala after rebuilding. Could fry the tires at will. Scary in the rain. <P>85 Fiero GT. First car that I ever bought new. <P>88 Firebird Formula (POS). Traded in the 85 GT, two weeks before they cancelled the Fiero. DOH!!!<P>88 Fiero coupe. Bought in December 97.<BR>Back into the Fiero obsession.<P>  <P> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||07-30-2001||09:54 AM||||Significant cars.<P>A 1972 Vega GT wagon..first new car biggest POS ever owned.  Body by rust.<P>1976 Nova Concourse second new car..350 4bbl 4 door sedan, a real sleeper and trouble free car.  Body by rust.<P>1978 VW Rabbit diesel, economical to run, expensive to repair.<P>1983 Pontiac 6000 LE, any component that held fluid, leaked.<P>1987 Fiero GT  5th new car, still have it, still most fun car.<P>1988 Fiero GT Money pit, everything has been replaced, should be a fine running machine.  I'll see on the trip to Williamsburg.<P>In between other cars 1976 Camaro.  The only thing that held the body together were the interior plastic body panels. Never had a car with rust holes through the roof before.<P>1984 Escort wagon.. A real basic used car, it had the radio delete option.  Ran well except a leaking o ring on the distributor which shorted out the distributor on a yearly basis.<P>1992 Suzuki Sidekick 4 door.   Economical SUV.  1.6 4 cylinder engine that revved forever.  Underpowered to the nth degree, but never broke down or required any special maintenance in 7 years of ownership.<P>1956 Ford wagon..blew the engine after 3 months of ownership.  100 mile per quart of oil.<P>1959 Plymouth Belvedere Convertible.  Only convertible owned.  Great for getting dust and dirt in your eyes when the top was down.  A high milage car when purchased, had transmission, engine , universals, shocks, replaced or rebuilt in 2 years of ownership.<P>1966 Pontiac Catalina 2 door sport coupe.  First nearly new car, trouble free 389 2bbl, that could smoke tires.  A real land barge by todays standards.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||saleenfiero||07-30-2001||11:43 AM||||1985 Chev Blazer 4X4:<BR>Typical for car, starting to rust bad, tired old 2.8, but who the hell cared, I was 17 and I had my first vehicle!<P>1985 Fiero SE:<BR>Beautiful little black fiero, great until the block cracked and the car was sold because I couldn't afford to fix it.<P>1985 Dodge Aries:<BR>Its an Aries, wow.<P>1989 Saleen Mustang:<BR>The only blue notchback Saleen they made that year, awesome car, super fast, guys loved it and girls dreamed of it (yeah right), total write off one night, from me being a little showy with the gas pedal.<P>1986 Fiero SE:<BR>The current project, total custom job, has the wing off the Saleen for a little different look.  Hopefully I will have nothing bad to say about this car<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula88||07-30-2001||01:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>76 Plymouth Roadrunner - first car<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>COOL!   A friend of mine in H.S. had a 76 Road Runner - 318, 2barrel, in that bright pumpkin orange (don't know the official name).  Did yours have the rear quarter window louvers?  I hear they were fairly rare.  I thought it was such a P.O.S. at the time, but would actually like to have one today.<P>My cars...<BR>'69 Firebird 350 - My first car.  Did my first carb and intake swap on this car - 2 to 4 barrel conversion.<P>'72 Trans Am - My first MUSCLE CAR.  Big block, oh YEAH!  Did my first engine swap in this one.  The 455HO spun a bearing, and since I couldn't afford to properly rebuild that engine, I purchased a shorblock from Racing Head Service in Memphis and rebuilt my round port heads for it.  When I sold the car, I made sure the original block went with it.  <P>'87 Grand National - My first new car.  Sold the Firebird to get the down payment.  Fun car, but it lacked the sould of the Pontiacs.  Couldn't argue with the straight line performance, but it just didn't have the feel.<P>'99 Grand Am - My first "practical" car.  ugh.  But, it's nice anyway.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>'88 Fiero Formula - My first FIERO!  And I'm sure not my last....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||07-30-2001||01:46 PM||||Most memorial?<P>1975 LT1 Camaro..  Got her when I was 16..<BR>Fun car.. really fast   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>1978 ford van..  factory customized..  this was my party van   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>- I got this when I was almost 18-<BR>After getting the van, I barely ever drove my camaro anymore hehe<P>(I still remember the time I got pulled over by the Cops and they stood there with their mouths open after 18 people climbed out of my van after leaving a party..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P><BR>and of course my fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  cause its so fun to drive..<P><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000012||fierosound||07-30-2001||08:02 PM||||My memorable cars...<P>1966 Barracuda Formula S - Commando 273 V8 4-speed w/side pipes (first car - WOW!) <BR>Dad me me get rid of it after cop followed me home to give me $hit for doing burnouts.<BR>1969 Camaro RS - 350 V8/auto, white leather interior (gorgeous)<BR>1972 Duster - 318/auto, not fast, but looked great in Fire Orange with Black stripes, Cragar spokes & BFGs<BR>1978 Pontiac Lemans Sport Coupe - 350 V8/auto, classy looking, great driver.<BR>1979 Chev Monza - 350/365HP V8 4-speed.  Very fast, Most guys shut down when they heard it tires squealing into 3rd gear.<BR>1987 Fiero GT (present car) <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm</A> <BR>Just done a major "rework" just this side of a restoration.  Good for another 15 years !!!||||reg||10
Z||000013||dlancer407||07-30-2001||10:48 PM||||First let me start by sayingI am 48 years old and my son and I were adding up all the cars I have owned in my life last week. We came up with 42 so far. When I look back over what I have owned there are a few I wish I had never sold.<P>1973 AMC JAVELIN AMX<BR>Bought in 1983, have owned longer than any other car, restored and have won many trophies. This one I don't think I will ever sell.<P>1988 CHEVY BERETTA GTU. Loved the looks of this car when I saw it at a Cincinnati new car expo, and had to have one. My car was photographed and appeared in Colectible Automobile Magazine in the early 90's as a future colectible.If you have the mags, it is White ( owned by Dennis Helferich )<P>1980 AMC SPIRT AMX. This was the last year for the AMX model. Only 865 built.<P>1987 Shelby Lancer #407. Another rare numbered car. Less than 800 built. Sold to my son last year, He loves this car.<P>1976 FORD MUSTANG COBRA II. The only Ford I have ever owned, and the biggest piece of S**T I have ever owned.<P>1985 PONTIAC FIERO GT. First 2 seat sports car, first car I have purchased off of Ebay,one of the most fun cars I have ever purchased.<P>1989 DODGE DAKOTA SPORT CONVERTIBLE. Super sharp, head turner, fun to drive.<P>I could go on and on but Cliff would kick my butt out of here.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||07-30-2001||11:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>Most memorial?<P>1975 LT1 Camaro..  Got her when I was 16..<BR>Fun car.. really fast    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Was that a "Type LT" or did you put an LT1 engine in it?  I always loved those mid 70s Camaros.  Better lines than the early or late 2nd gens, IMO.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||KRMFiero||07-30-2001||11:37 PM||||1986 Ford Escort /w 5 speed<BR>well its the only other one besides Fiero's I loved that car my dad let me buy it when i turned 14 for 500$, everyday for over a year i would back down the end of my driveway, rev it to redline and dump the clutch, bring it in to second still spinning, if it was rainging 3rd or sometimes 4th  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i did it a good 20-30 times a day for like a whole summer stright and then a few times a day after the summer, i took it to the sand pits a few times and well lets just say i beat the hell of that car i took it though trails and eveything, took it mudding... i sold last year for 200$ to my friend that had no clue how to drive stick, he learned on it - beat the hell out of it and mostly the clutch and he gave it to his grandfather who drove it for a week and sold it for 500$ to a member on my Fire Dept who drives it 50 miles to work everyday and back, i think that is pretty good for what it is i mean its probley a stock clutch I sold it cause i thought it was going to fall apart any second  it still runs great, i changed the oil every 2 weeks (I let it like idle over night and stuff i sleeped in it; needed heat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">)  well  think it is significant becuase well it still runs great, i dont see how hehe i held that thing floored with it in nutral and nothing happined<P>anyways i liked it hehe<BR>Kyle<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||maryjane||07-31-2001||02:58 AM||||Well, they were all significant inasmuch as they kept me from walkin. But...<BR>61 vette I bought with money I saved while in VietNam-learned just how many speeding tickets you can get before they pull your license.,also know very well how many pieces a powerglide tranny can fly into:neutral-redline-drive=disaster. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>84 se I have now<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||1
Z||000017||onfire||07-31-2001||04:23 AM||||1. 1978 Trans-Am. My very first car I was buying it from my uncle. It was voted one of the top five cars in high school. I had that car upto 145 m.p.h. or so, going to Seattle. Due to family problems, I moved to Spokane. My uncle got the car back, I only owed him like $500. <P>2. 1969 El Camino. Had that car er truck for about 9 months. I was rear ended by a drunk driver. The engine and tranny lived on in a friends nova.<P>3. 198? Suburu Justy with front end damage. I had this car for 2 weeks. I bought it for $200. The last day of its life consisted of a 400 mile roadtrip. The clutch went out the last 100 miles or so. Sunday about 3:00 a.m. in the snow over a mountain pass in second gear almost the whole way home. I killed it at a red light. Me and my friend that was with me, had to push it the last 2 blocks. Sold it for $150 to a junk yard.<P>4. 1985 Fiero GT. The first car I bought from a dealer with my own credit. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I miss this car the most. Me and my uncle were out drinking one night. To make a long story short. We ended up sideways in a ditch. The car was never the same after that. Needless to say I'm not a good drunk driver. (p.s. I don't drink and drive anymore). We did get the car together again. But it spun a bearing about 6 months later. We replaced it, but it only lasted about 20 miles. So I sold it.<P>5. 1986 Chevy S10 4x4. My first 4x4. Plus I still own it.<P>6. 1985 Fiero GT #2. I just got this car. It won't be driven to much til sometime next year. It will soon be at my friends shop, and he will be getting alot of my money, and help from me. I had so many plans for the first Fiero that didn't get done. So this time I have a plan, and I'm sticking to it.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Fierowrecker||07-31-2001||06:27 AM||||My most memorable cars...<P>My first car, a 1968 Chevy Malibu, totaled out on Christmas eve, one year after purchase...<P>My second car, a 1963 Ford Galaxy station wagon to replace my totaled 68 Malibu, and the first car to get laid in...<P>My third car, a 1963 Chevy Nova 4 door POS that I modified by dropping in a 340 Buick engine, 15 second quarter mile, a warmed over 350 SB, 14 second quarter mile, and a realy warmed over 350 SB, 13 second quarter mile, had this car the longest, 19 years, totaled it and myself...<P>My fifth (skipping the fourth), my 84 2M4 Fiero, still have, just rusted out...<P>And my sixth, seventh and eighth, all Fieros, and I still have them!<P>I have had trucks, vans, and a motor home, but they arn't cars...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000019||Fiero_24||07-31-2001||08:12 AM||||I love Fiero's, and I have yet to own a really nice one (until my hopped up V6 gets finished).  Here is a URL of my 2 seater Camaro that was a Factory authorized conversion, like the T-top Fiero.  I bought this car about 6 years ago and have won a few car shows with it.  The car is a big mystery with the Callaway markings and the moulded Callaway door handles.  Everything I know about the car is what I have heard from other owners. <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fieroproject/forsale.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fieroproject/forsale.html</A> <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||12
Z||000020||isthiswhereiputausername?||07-31-2001||08:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Was that a "Type LT" or did you put an LT1 engine in it?  I always loved those mid 70s Camaros.  Better lines than the early or late 2nd gens, IMO.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Type LT..   she died of rust at the end  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Still have the  emblems,taillights  and glass off it  if you know anyone interested<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||firstfiero||07-31-2001||09:12 AM||||   I've had many cars...but a short list of the one's that mattered..<BR>  1)77 porsche 924- my baby...bought it with a blown engine. My dad and I replaced it and drove for one summer befor I started having electrical problems. That's when the divorce came and I couldn't afford 65 bucks an hour for the porsche man to search down the problem. Had to sell it.<BR>  2)80 bmw 528i-A car like our fiero. All the bmw drivers would turn their nose up to you because it wasn't a well liked car. I think they looked better then any 5 series made. That 4 door sedan could out handle my porsche or fiero. It stuck like glue!! The rust monster was eating her and right when I was deciding if I should put thousands into her or sell it my best friend called and offered me for 500 buck his......<BR>  3)86 fiero se- My favorite car I've ever owned. It's fast, it handles well and it's absolutly beautiful. Add to the fact the parts are cheap and personally I think it adds up to one of best buys for the buck for the average joe to have. Got<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||TSPalmer||07-31-2001||09:48 AM||||This is weird, I was trying to remember all the cars I've owned on the way to work this morning!  Good thing I was practicing...LOL<P>Anyway, here goes...<P>72 Mach I - (almost dead 302) cost a whole $150.00 then all the repairs and paint, bought a 71 Thunderbird for the 429 (Holley 750 4bbl, C6 auto)to drop in the Mach and sold the T-Bird for scrap.<P>80 Fiat X1/9 - Traded the Mach for this mistake...I could drive home from school and then had to wait 30 minutes before it would crank again. It rusted in the yard for years and finally sold it for $400.00.<P>73 Mustang - White Grande with a green vinyl top. 351C with 2bbl. Problems and more problems...<P>71 Mustang - Traded the 73 to my soon to be father-in-law for the red 71 he had been tinkering with.  351C 4bbl and a hand choke. Stuck it in a ditch showing off for the female passenger that wasn't my gf......ooops<P>72 SuperBeetle - Fun but had all ready been dogged before I got it, at least it got me through getting the 71 Mustang painted....<P>87 Suzuki Samurai JX - What the he?? was I thinking?  It lasted long enough to be traded in on a brand new...<P>90 Probe GL - My first new car.  When I traded it in, it had 116,000 miles on it.<P>91 Honda Civic - Bought for the sheer purpose of being driven into the ground.  My Dad now has it with over 216,000 miles on it for his daily driver.<P>92 Probe GT - Great car, way too fast for my own good (reliving Mach I days).  Had a bad habit of blowing the hose from the turbo to the intake manifold off at the worst times.<P>85 Fiero SE - My first Fiero, it's a work in process.  I'm the 3rd owner, first drove it through a fence and sold it to owner #2.  He didn't have a problem with the scars and left it as is.  Clutch problems/shift cable problems, paint is shot, sunroof glass is even scratched, but I love the car.<P>89 Honda CRX Si - couldn't resist, it goes so well with the Fiero.  My friend keeps telling me that I'm trying to complete the collection of cars we wanted back in high school days.  It's my daily beater so I don't wear the Fiero out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry so long...<BR><P>------------------<BR>T.Shawn Palmer<BR>'85 SE 4cyl 5spd||||reg||12
Z||000023||FLASHY||07-31-2001||12:42 PM||||Here's the only other car I've owned. I sure do miss it. But hey, I sold it to get my fiero so there's a plus.<P>'76 VW Beetle<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mybug1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flashy_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||1
Z||000024||rogergarrison||07-31-2001||02:17 PM||||My 'most' signif was prob my 63 Plymouth Valient convertible. My first real project car. Painted black with rainbow metalflake and flames around the front. Bubble in hood. Interior was diamond stitched in blue metalflake vinyl. Engine was a 69 Superbee 426 Hemi with cross ram carbs, pushbutton torqueflite 727 (?) I never had any trouble at all except once twisted the rear pinion out racing a GTO. Ran like a bat out of h__l. It would smoke tires for a block. bottom of rear bumper was scraped off prob an inch from red lite wheelstands. Def a fun ride.||||reg||1
Z||000025||bHooper||07-31-2001||02:47 PM||||i have owned:<BR>1st car: <BR>1977 toyota celica- what a piece of junk that car was, but at leat i couldn't kill myself!<P>1980 toyota corolla sr5- this was a 3 door car.  it was sporty 9or at least i thought so, having come from the celica.  it was black with orange plastic stripping... we called the crayolla or the godzilla mobile.<P>1987 honda crx- this was my first new car.  what a blast!  i used to drive that thing through the gravel mountain roads (at college) pretending i was some great european rally driver!<P>1986- pontiac fiero GT- still own that car... nuf said? nope, awesome ride, and better after i spent $1300 on the suspension last year!  now it needs paint.<P>1991- mazda rx7- i really wanted one of the 3rd generation cars, but instead i wound up with the last of the 2nd... and an automatic to boot!  never buy a wankle powered car that doesnt have a straight drive!<P>1998- jeep cherkee- my 2nd new vehicle.  great fun, lots of power, can go anywhere and carry nearly anything.  only problem, it doesn't have a moveable rear window (never understood that).<P>1986 pontiac fiero SE- i just got this one.  bought it sight unsean (well Doug did send me a video tape of it).  it's a good car.  i got it because i wanted an automatic for a daily driver.<P>next car?! dont know.  i like the new celica's, miata's, bmw z3 coupe's, s2000's; but i am also interested in 65 t bird convertible's and old british roadsters! <P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
